PART 2 — NEW EDITOR CODE (added in this fork)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Project:   Quarkdown Live Editor
  Author:    Luiz Rodolfo (Thedocwhocode) <luizrodolfocc@gmail.com>
  Source:    https://github.com/Thedocwhocode/quarkdown-live-editor
  Copyright: Copyright (C) 2025 Luiz Rodolfo (Thedocwhocode)
  License:   GNU General Public License v3.0

The following directory was written from scratch for this fork and was NOT
present in the upstream project:

  editor/                       Structured live editor (React + TypeScript)
    ├── server.ts               Node.js / Express compile proxy API
    ├── src/core/ir/            Intermediate representation (IR/AST) types
    ├── src/core/registry/      Quarkdown function registry (30+ stdlib entries)
    ├── src/core/serializer/    Deterministic IR → .qd source serializer
    ├── src/core/parser/        Best-effort .qd → IR parser
    ├── src/core/compiler-adapter/   HTTP adapter to the compile API
    ├── src/features/document/  Zustand document state store
    ├── src/features/preview/   Preview orchestrator (debounce + compile)
    ├── src/features/source-sync/    Bidirectional IR ↔ source sync
    └── src/components/         React UI components
          app-shell/            Three-panel shell layout
          toolbar/              Quick-insert toolbar
          block-library/        Searchable block catalog panel
          editor-surface/       Block-based writing surface
          document-setup/       Document metadata form
          inspector/            Selection inspector panel
          source-view/          CodeMirror 6 source editor panel
          preview/              Live HTML preview pane (iframe)
          diagnostics/          Compiler error display panel

This editor code is a derivative work of Quarkdown. It integrates with the
Quarkdown compiler by spawning the CLI as a subprocess through the Express
proxy server. The IR, registry, serializer, and parser are original
implementations written to interoperate with Quarkdown's syntax and stdlib.


